 Montgomery County","/arc-plc/alabama/montgomery-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids has come in under 90% of normal in April to May 37 times in 75 years, the most of any pair. In 2025, September to October came in at 44% of normal on the middle of the grids, and October to November at 49%. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 14575 down to 49% of normal. Grid 14576 shows a preliminary estimate of 62.9 for July to August 2026.</p>"}
